Z||000003||TwisT||03-07-2001||07:31 PM||||Awwwwwwww drooooooool!<P>This is cool as sh!t to see,  as this is my future motor install.  <P>I've had lot's of experience with a supercharged V6,  though not of GM nature.  My experience comes from my previously owned '91 Thunderbird SC.  With just some high-flow mods,  you can make these suckers MOVE.  Make 'em breathe and HOLD ON!<P>I assume the basics would apply to the Fiero as well.  High-flow exhaust...  low-restriction intake...  then the supercharger pulley,  in that order.  Not sure about the GM unit,  but it advised to install the pulley AFTER you open up the exhaust,  as the increased levels of boost can blow your head gaskets REAL quick.  Gearing is the next step,  though not sure which combo would work best in the Fiero.<P>Would be interesting to learn the specifics of this particular Fiero set-up.  Which tranny is being used?  What other mods to the motor were made?<P>Droooooooooool!<P>Brett||||reg||1
